{"name":"Broom","hex":"#eecc24","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Broom","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A number of places in England:\nA village in Southill parish, Central Bedfordshire district, Bedfordshire .\nA hamlet in Long Marton parish, Eden district, Cumbria .\nA locality in Thorncombe parish, west Dorset, on the boundary with Devon and close to Somerset . \nA southern suburb of Rotherham, South Yorkshire .\nA village in Bidford-on-Avon parish, Stratford-on-Avon district, Warwickshire .","A village in Southill parish, Central Bedfordshire district, Bedfordshire ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Broom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Broom","blocks":[{"text":"A broom, also known as a broomstick, is a cleaning tool, consisting of usually stiff fibers attached to, and roughly parallel to, a cylindrical handle, the broomstick. It is thus a variety of brush with a long handle. It is commonly used in combination with a dustpan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/BroomsforSale.jpg/330px-BroomsforSale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Broom","wikidata":"Q172833"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Broom_Han_Dynasty_British_Museum_MAS.776.jpg/500px-Broom_Han_Dynasty_British_Museum_MAS.776.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Broom_Han_Dynasty_British_Museum_MAS.776.jpg/1280px-Broom_Han_Dynasty_British_Museum_MAS.776.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Broom_Han_Dynasty_British_Museum_MAS.776.jpg/500px-Broom_Han_Dynasty_British_Museum_MAS.776.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Broom excavated from Dunhuang, China, da